{0 tb_ocaml}

Prototype-grade TigerBeetle-compatible server and CLI in OCaml.

The codebase is intentionally split around a small typed core:

- {!module-U128} defines the 128-bit values used for identifiers, amounts, and checksums.
- {!module-Types} centralizes protocol constants and ledger-facing records.
- {!module-Multibatch} implements the batch trailer format used by request and reply payloads.
- {!module-Codec} maps between typed values and the binary wire protocol.
- {!module-State} owns persistence and ledger validation rules.
- {!module-Server} and {!module-Repl} keep effects at the edge.

The Dune documentation flow for this package is:

{[
  dune build @doc
]}

Generated HTML is written under:

{[
  _build/default/_doc/_html/
]}

Examples in the module interfaces mirror the executable tests in:

- [tests/unit_tests.ml]
- [tests/property_tests.ml]
- [tests/cli.t]

That keeps the docs honest: examples are short on purpose and should describe
the same shapes the test suite relies on.
